{
  "task_description": "{'component_name': 'Main Container for CityFix Hub', 'description': 'Primary container for CityFix Hub implementation: Fix the City is a web platform for citizens to report public issues (like potholes, waste, illegal parking, etc.) by uploading a photo, description, and location. Reports are stored in MongoDB, photos in Cloudinary, and users/admins can track and update issue statuses. The app is built with a React frontend and Node.js/Express backend, designed for easy deployment and mobile usability.', 'interfaces': [], 'framework': 'react', 'platform': 'web', 'container': '{\n  "name": "CityFix Hub-27305 frontend Container",\n  "features": [\n    {\n      "name": "Issue Reporting",\n      "description": "Users can report public issues by selecting a type, adding a description, uploading a photo, and automatically capturing GPS location.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Photo Upload",\n      "description": "Photos are uploaded to Cloudinary and linked to each report.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Location Capture",\n      "description": "Uses browser Geolocation API to capture and store the location of the reported issue.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Report Status Tracking",\n      "description": "Users can view all reports and their statuses (Reported, In Progress, Fixed).",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Admin Status Update",\n      "description": "Admins can update the status of any report via the UI.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Responsive UI",\n      "description": "The website is mobile-friendly and user-friendly, with error handling for common issues.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "API Integration",\n      "description": "Frontend communicates with backend via Axios, with CORS enabled.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    },\n    {\n      "name": "Deployment Ready",\n      "description": "Project is structured for deployment on Vercel, with environment variables for sensitive data.",\n      "isEnabled": true\n    }\n  ],\n  "techStack": {\n    "frontend": [\n      "React JS"\n    ],\n    "backend": [\n      "None"\n    ],\n    "language": [\n      "JavaScript (ES6+)"\n    ]\n  },\n  "colors": {\n    "primary": "#ffffff",\n    "secondary": "#0000ff",\n    "accent": "#00ff00"\n  },\n  "theme": "dark",\n  "layoutDescription": "The UI features a top navigation bar with the project title. The main area has a form for submitting new issues (dropdown for type, text area for description, photo upload, and location capture). Below, a responsive grid displays all reported issues as cards, each showing the photo, type, description, location (as coordinates), status, and admin action buttons. Error and success messages are shown as banners or toasts. The layout adapts for mobile screens."\n}'}",
